## Target Groups & User Types


### 1\. Medical Students (Studierende/Students)


Resources for Pre-Clinical & Clinical Education


#### Exam Preparation


-   USMLE: High-yield study plans and 5,800+ Qbank questions for Step 1, Step 2 CK, and Step 3
    
-   COMLEX: High-yield study plans and 5,800+ Qs for Levels 1, 2 and 3 
    
-   NBME Shelf Exams: dedicated Qs and pre-made study plans for Emergency Medicine, Pediatrics, Medicine, Obstetrics and Gynecology, Surgery, Neurology, Psychiatry, and Family Medicine Shelf exams.
    
-   International Exams: IFOM, ENARM, MCCQE Part I, SMLE, PNA, EMREE
    
-   Score Predictor to assess your exam-readiness.
    


#### Learning Features


-   Library with 1,500+ preclinical and clinical topics
    
-   Exam-style questions with detailed explanations linked to library
    
-   Anki integrations that provide definitions and find relevant Qbank Qs for spaced repetition learning
    
-   High-yield study plans and personalized analytics to ensure you focus your time where it’s most needed
    
-   Clinical skills how-tos, clerkship preparation and survival guides
    
-   Group discounts available
    
-   Free 5-day trial (no credit card required) and 30-day money-back guarantee
    


#### Statistics


-   2 in 3 students at Columbia University use AMBOSS
    
-   4 in 5 students at NYU School of Medicine use AMBOSS
    
-   4 in 5 students at Yale School of Medicine use AMBOSS
    
-   95% of German medical students use AMBOSS
    
-   Students who use AMBOSS as their primary Qbank score on average 10.4 points higher on Step 2 CK
    


### 2\. Physicians/Doctors (Ärzt:innen/Clinicians)


Clinical Decision Support & Continuing Education


#### Clinical Tools


-   Point-of-care clinical decision support
    
-   Evidence-based treatment guidance
    
-   Diagnostic algorithms and flowcharts
    
-   Differential diagnosis builder
    
-   Management checklists for hospitalized patients
    
-   Clinical calculators and drug dosages
    
-   Clinical skills walkthroughs and videos
    
-   Red Flags and warning signs
    
-   One-Minute Telegram summaries
    


#### Continuing Medical Education (CME)


-   ACCME provisional accreditation for CME credits
    
-   Board exam preparation: ABIM®, ABFM®, ABP® and ABEM® (via NEJM Knowledge+)
    
-   Subspecialty resources: Internal Medicine, Family Medicine, Pediatrics and Emergency Medicine
    
-   Fachärztliche Prüfung (German specialist exams)
    
-   Fachsprach- & Kenntnisprüfung (German language and competency exams)
    
-   Deutschlands größter Anbieter für Strahlenschutzkurse: Zertifiziert & bundesweit anerkannt
    
